# Findings reviewed and dismissed, by fingerprint.
#
# Each line names one finding in one commit at one line, so dismissing it says
# nothing about any other. The rule itself stays as sharp as it was: the point
# of `mtproto-secret` is to stop sixteen bytes of hexadecimal from being
# committed, and it should go on doing that.
#
# These six are a made-up sponsorship tag written out as a literal in the tests
# that introduced `AdTag`. They were never issued by anyone and never worked.
# The literals are gone from the tree — the tests build the tag now, the way
# they already built client secrets — but they remain in the commit that added
# them, and a scan of the history still reaches them.
#
# Rewriting the history to erase a tag that was never real would cost more than
# it is worth. Naming them here is the honest record: reviewed, understood,
# left alone.

